<p>President Trump said he is postponing a planned trip to China by about five or six weeks so he can stay in Washington as the war involving Iran continues. The visit had been expected around the end of March and was set to include a meeting in Beijing with Chinese President Xi Jinping, part of a broader push to ease tensions between the world’s two largest economies. The White House said the delay reflects the immediate demands of the Middle East conflict, not a breakdown in U.S.-China contacts. Chinese officials said Beijing and Washington remain in touch about the visit, and Trump said China was “fine” with the change — a small sign that both sides still want the summit to happen once the regional crisis eases.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/pTCn8AOL-jmzWzpDGLToPn8u_6fRAxzjz8hybTAL7cn7Yle638WOYB_3yhpYlaZ_XqJvLhjMUoIo7c4wguEdZpsmFS6jiQLpUhsY0iEiwU9vYcBgHzu9tyxalah5Gj-eV98vpzZenhnYWYdJrdCs2Uf7UDL7qkMtSkxH-AErQskMGROnETAeIDA_QirHa6-nA3nNB35vEV8q1Zb7PoilXYjRnb6vrOjBH9ec84ofmOqZ_F4vrCQXCddkbkJS6Ayv9Lsa59Wz30e7ikBAQg' alt='U.S. President Donald Trump speaks during a meeting with Taoiseach of Ireland Micheál Martin in the Oval Office of the White House on March 17, 2026 in Washington, DC.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Earlier linkage: Before the postponement, Trump had suggested his Beijing visit could depend on whether China helped Washington reopen the Strait of Hormuz, showing how the Iran conflict was already spilling into summit planning.</li><li>Conflict spillover: The delay came as the U.S.-Israel war against Iran entered its third week, underscoring how the crisis is disrupting diplomacy far beyond the Middle East.</li><li>Long-planned trip: The China visit had been in the works for months before the regional war forced a rethink, highlighting how quickly the White House’s foreign-policy agenda shifted.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Trump said he was not &quot;trying to play games&quot; with Beijing by postponing the trip and cast the request as a wartime scheduling decision, not a diplomatic slight. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983256/china-says-delay-in-trump-visit-not-linked-to-hormuz-closure'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Chinese Foreign Ministry: Spokesman Lin Jian said Beijing had noted U.S. clarifications that reports linking the visit delay to Hormuz were inaccurate and added that both countries remain in communication about the trip. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983256/china-says-delay-in-trump-visit-not-linked-to-hormuz-closure'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Chinese embassy in Washington: The embassy did not endorse Trump’s proposed timetable and said it had no new information about when the summit might happen. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-expects-xi-summit-in-five-or-six-weeks-as-iran-war-rages'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/trump-delays-china-trip-until-next-month-to-focus-on-the-war-in-iran'>Trump postpones China trip to focus on war in Iran</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-expects-xi-summit-in-five-or-six-weeks-as-iran-war-rages'>Trump expects Xi summit in ‘five or six weeks’ as Iran war rages</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1rwvsft/china_ignores_trumps_hormuz_request_as_the_iran/'>China ignores Trump’s Hormuz request as the Iran war deepens and his Beijing trip slips</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-trump-postpones-china-trip-iran-war-strait-of-hormuz/'>Trump postpones China trip to focus on Iran war</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/03/18/gbak-m18.html'>Trump calls for a delay in summit with Chinese president</a> - wsws.org</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/article/3346937/trump-confirms-delay-beijing-meeting-xi-amid-iran-conflict'>Trump confirms dela